# CMB Power Spectrum catalogue --- full Planck PR3 / R3.01 binned TT ingest.
# Each line below is one MPR row data block (NDJSON).
# Lines starting with "#" or empty lines are skipped by the
# literature_curated adapter.
#
# Single row_type "multipole_bin" catalogue (111 rows): TT-only full coverage
# spanning ell=2-2499. This commit replaces the prior 15-row representative
# seed with the complete Planck PR3 / R3.01 binned TT spectrum.
#
#   - Low-ell rows (ell=2..29, 28 rows, ell_half_width=0):
#       Planck 2018 Commander likelihood, file
#       COM_PowerSpect_CMB-TT-full_R3.01.txt (unbinned per-ell values).
#       Asymmetric -dDl / +dDl errors from PR3 release; we record both
#       (D_ell_error_minus_muK2, D_ell_error_plus_muK2) plus a
#       symmetrized value in D_ell_error_muK2 (mean of -/+ for the
#       schema-required field).
#
#   - High-ell rows (ell~47..2499, 83 binned bands, ell_half_width~10-16):
#       Planck 2018 Plik likelihood, file
#       COM_PowerSpect_CMB-TT-binned_R3.01.txt. Bin half-widths computed
#       from adjacent-bin-center midpoints (Plik uses dl~30 binning above
#       ell=30, slightly wider in the first and last bins). Symmetric
#       Gaussian errors. lcdm_bestfit_D_ell_muK2 records the published
#       LambdaCDM best-fit at the bin center as a reference column.
#
# Feature labelling reflects the actual Planck PR3 peak/trough locations:
#   1st peak ell~225, 1st trough ell~405, 2nd peak ell~525,
#   2nd trough ell~675, 3rd peak ell~825, damping tail beyond.
# Low-ell anomaly window restricted to ell in [2, 5] (suppressed
# quadrupole + octupole alignment, the canonical "Axis of Evil" regime).
#
# Source provenance: Planck Collaboration 2018 VI (Aghanim et al. 2020,
# A&A 641:A6, doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201833910) is cited per-row as the
# canonical published-result reference. The PR3 / R3.01 likelihood
# release tables are documented in Planck 2018 V (Akrami et al. 2020
# A&A 641:A5) and distributed via the Planck Legacy Archive at
# https://pla.esac.esa.int/. Each row records its source_file
# (COM_PowerSpect_CMB-TT-full_R3.01.txt or
# COM_PowerSpect_CMB-TT-binned_R3.01.txt) for byte-level traceability;
# follow-up ingest can attach response_sha256 attestations against the
# actual downloaded bytes.
#
# precision_flag = "high" for all rows --- values are taken directly from
# the published PR3 tables without rounding.

